00:52:26,990 --> 00:52:32,112
And now you can see a list of all of these different Pokemons that we're fetching from an API.

554
00:52:32,352 --> 00:52:34,628
This is pretty amazing, isn't it?

555
00:52:35,214 --> 00:52:41,552
We're fetching this data directly within the route itself in such a simple and intuitive way.

556
00:52:41,774 --> 00:52:45,632
Keep in mind that this loader runs before the component renders.

557
00:52:45,838 --> 00:52:52,164
So whatever you return here in the loader is available in the component via the use loader data hook.

558
00:52:52,654 --> 00:52:53,156
That's it.

559
00:52:53,582 --> 00:52:54,432
Super simple.

560
00:52:54,734 --> 00:52:57,380
But Tanstack makes it even easier.

561
00:52:57,934 --> 00:53:08,032
In the same route, Tanstack allows you to define pending states, components for error, for not found, and even allow you to validate your request using Zod

562
00:53:08,352 --> 00:53:12,612
before even making a request, all attached to your route file.

563
00:53:12,832 --> 00:53:19,072
So let me quickly show you how that works, then we'll dive a bit deeper into it while you're developing the skills application.

564
00:53:19,310 --> 00:53:26,272
