because with it, you'll also join the waitlist for the full Tanstack course that I'm actively working on.

566
00:53:32,432 --> 00:53:34,916
So let's first talk about pending states.

567
00:53:35,342 --> 00:53:38,628
See, when you fetch data, there is always a delay.

568
00:53:39,182 --> 00:53:46,852
And instead of showing a blank white screen until the data arrives, you want to show a loading spinner or a skeleton UI.

569
00:53:47,152 --> 00:53:52,004
Because Tanstack Router handles this beautifully with pending component functionality.

570
00:53:52,352 --> 00:54:01,604
So right here, above or below the loader, you can specify the pending component and then define it right here by returning it.

571
00:54:01,998 --> 00:54:06,660
Let's say that it is a div, and this div will have a class name of

572
00:54:07,918 --> 00:54:13,792
P14 text-center and it'll say loading Pokemon.

573
00:54:14,158 --> 00:54:25,232
Now, in an ideal world, this wouldn't just be the text, it would be a skeleton component that nicely shimmers and specifies that something is about to come on the screen.

574
00:54:25,422 --> 00:54:33,392
And even better, you can also include the pending MS. So if your data loads incredibly fast, like under one second by default,

575
00:54:33,552 --> 00:54:36,356
it won't flash that jarring loading spinner on the user.

576
00:54:36,654 --> 00:54:40,068
It'll only show the pending UI if the network is actually slow.

577
00:54:40,352 --> 00:54:47,632
So you can say something like 300 milliseconds, which means that it'll wait 300 milliseconds before showing the loading state.

578
00:54:47,790 --> 00:54:51,556
So now we know how you can display some kind of skeletons while the content is loading.

579
00:54:51,952 --> 00:54:54,244
Then we also have error handling.

580
00:54:54,606 --> 00:55:03,620
So for any errors happening in that route, you can define a separate, specific or reusable component that renders when the error does happen.

581
00:55:03,854 --> 00:55:11,268
Again, you can do it on top or below, but basically you do it by defining the error component in the same way as before.

582
00:55:11,534 --> 00:55:16,292
And you can render some kind of a div that has a class name set to

583
00:55:17,102 --> 00:55:20,260
p14 text dash red 500.

584
00:55:20,718 --> 00:55:27,552
And you can display some kind of an error message like p tag that says oops, error happened.

