00:55:47,438 --> 00:55:52,388
Well, to do that, you can accept the actual error object within the error component.

590
00:55:52,782 --> 00:55:57,988
And we can also get access to the router functionality by saying use router right here.

591
00:55:58,286 --> 00:56:07,312
But make sure to make this not an immediate return, rather just a regular return, rather, just a regular function, and then return this div

592
00:56:07,552 --> 00:56:08,036
manually.

593
00:56:08,494 --> 00:56:12,672
And make sure to import the use router coming from TanStack React router.

594
00:56:13,134 --> 00:56:20,324
What this allows us to do is to specify which error happened by getting access to its error message,

595
00:56:21,006 --> 00:56:23,952
such as oops, API is down.

596
00:56:24,494 --> 00:56:28,132
Maybe we can make this a bit less threatening of a color.

