639
01:00:11,342 --> 01:00:20,032
Well, in simple terms, it means you can execute a function that lives on a completely different computer, like your server,

640
01:00:20,432 --> 01:00:25,188
exactly as if it were a normal local function in your front-end code.

641
01:00:25,632 --> 01:00:33,700
You don't have to write any manual fetch requests, define URL endpoints, set headers, or parse JSON responses.

642
01:00:34,062 --> 01:00:43,232
The framework handles all of that messy HTTP plumbing automatically while keeping your TypeScript types perfectly intact from back

643
01:00:43,406 --> 01:00:44,068
to front.

644
01:00:44,352 --> 01:00:51,684
And if you've been around the React ecosystem, you've almost certainly heard about the term TRPC.

645
01:00:52,270 --> 01:01:00,228
It's a massively popular standalone library designed to give developers this exact type safe RPC experience.

646
01:01:00,622 --> 01:01:09,124
But the beautiful thing about Tanstack Start is that it has this TRPC style architecture built natively into the framework

647
01:01:09,472 --> 01:01:10,724
via server functions.

648
01:01:11,278 --> 01:01:21,072
So you get this incredible developer experience and end-to-end type safety of TRPC without having to install or configure a separate library.

